<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Intentionally minimal / empty.

      DeviceDiag must NOT be sandboxed: LogArchiveService.swift and
      AnalysisEngine.swift shell out to /usr/bin/tar, /usr/bin/log, and
      /usr/bin/plutil via Process. App Sandbox blocks spawning arbitrary
      subprocesses (or requires per-tool temporary-exception entitlements
      that are fragile and version-dependent) — so do not add:

          <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
          <true/>

      Hardened Runtime is enabled at sign time via `codesign --options
      runtime` (see build_app.sh), which is required for notarization. This
      file doesn't request any of the optional hardened-runtime exceptions
      (disable-library-validation, allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory,
      etc.) because nothing in the app needs them. If a future change adds a
      dependency that does, add the specific entitlement key here rather than
      broadening this.

      Reading user-selected sysdiagnose files (via the NSOpenPanel or
      drag-and-drop in UploadView.swift) does not need a special entitlement
      either — macOS treats explicit user selection (open panel, drag/drop)
      as implicit consent even for protected folders like ~/Desktop or
      ~/Downloads, for both sandboxed and non-sandboxed apps.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
